pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression: a CHECKED core deletion whose obligation the kernel discharges.
% Constraint 3 (`x2 >= 1`) is implied by 1 and 2, so `del id 3;` takes the RUP
% path of `check_checked_deletion` -- which runs with `only_core = true` and
% AFTER the constraint is removed, so the database it refutes `~c` against is
% exactly `setNone i CO`, the hypothesis of `VeriPbCore.dbBack_delete_checked`.
% The backward invariant therefore survives this deletion, and with no
% exclusion and no bound the forward half goes through too, so the run reports
% nothing outside the proved fragment.
f 3;
del id 3;
output EQUISATISFIABLE FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
